            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous hematoma of the abdominal wall.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>15-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the differential diagnosis of the acute abdomen, the possibility should be considered of a hematoma in the anterior abdominal wall, especially if the patient is a woman of advanced age with abdominal scars, with a chronic cough and on anticoagulant treatment. Cystography is valuable as a supplementary method of examination.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
